\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol A Bit Stronger\b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2011\par 22:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indices ended lower Thursday, as some weaknesses in international markets and softer or volatile metals prices drove various blue chip shares down.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General index closed down by 0.56% at 22861.64. The Selective blue-chip index was also down by 0.93%, to close at 31151.87, while the key mining subindex lost 0.17%.\par \par \uc2 Gold miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura SA\uc2  (BVN, BUENAVC1.Vl) lost 3.91%, in line with softer gold prices, to close at $40.60.\par \par \uc2 Base metals miner \uc2 Compania Minera Milpo\uc2  SAA (MILPOC1.VL) was down 0.69% to close at 7.18 soles ($2.59). Also losing value, on volatile red metal prices, was copper miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO, SCCO.VL), down 0.11% to close at $44.70.\par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) gained 1.12% in busy trade to close at $50.51.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday to buy $93 million at an average of PEN2.766 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol ended slightly stronger at PEN2.767 to the dollar from PEN2.769 to the dollar at the previous session's close. Over the last 12-month period the sol has appreciated by 3.12% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 With Thursday's purchase, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has now \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  four times so far this year to purchase dollars.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased dollars regularly last year to smooth out volatility in the exchange market, as the sol has been on an appreciating trend. Last year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $8.96 billion.\par \par \uc2 -By Sophie Kevany, Dow Jones Newswires; 51(1)-989 038 043; sophie.kevany@dowjones.com [ 02-10-11 1645ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110210e72a000ds\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
