\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes Ends Higher; Sol Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2011\par 23:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indices ended higher Wednesday as some blue-chip miners posted gains.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General Index closed up 0.87% at 23419.93. The blue-chip Selective Index rose 0.85% to close at 32126.74, while the key mining subindex gained 0.85%.\par \par \uc2 Rising was silver miner Sociedad Minera El Brocal SAA (BROCALC1.VL), as silver made gains earlier in the day. It gained 3.39% to close at 57.90 soles ($20.90). Also gaining, on higher tin prices, was tin miner \uc2 Minsur SA\uc2  (MINSURI1.VL), which ended 3.12% higher at PEN4.60.\par \par \uc2 Going the other way was financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP), which fell 0.46% to $108.10. Credicorp owns Peru's biggest bank, Banco de Credito.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday to buy $97 million at an average rate of PEN2.766 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which purchased dollars regularly last year to smooth out volatility in the exchange market, also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, buying $18 million. Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the first since October.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol has been appreciating recently due in part to strong inflows of capital. Last year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a total of $8.96 billion.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday the sol ended unchanged at PEN2.767 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 So far this year the sol has appreciated 1.43% against the dollar, while in the last 12 months it has appreciated 2.95% against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 -By Sophie Kevany, Dow Jones Newswires; 51(1)-989 038 043; sophie.kevany@dowjones.com [ 02-02-11 1717ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110202e722000fc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
