argest Aaa country, expects to return to a balanced budged by 2014-2015 and its banking system remains strong, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fiscal metrics for Australia and Singapore, in particular, are among the strongest of Aaa-rated sovereigns, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said, pointing out that Singapore "is currently not in any need of large-scale structural fiscal adjustments."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's debt position "also compares favourably with the [Aaa] group" although the central government's net debt is projected to rise from a low of around 6% of gross domestic product in 2008 to nearly 30% in 2015, before declining.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But these are well below median government debt levels for Aaa countries, and New Zealand's strong banking system means the contingent liability on the government balance sheet is small, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Even with some further slippage... from slower growth or other one-time shocks, it appears highly likely that these ratios will remain within the stronger side of the Aaa range."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Mark Brown, Dow Jones Newswires, + 44 (0)207 842 9485;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 mark.brown@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1700 GMT [Dow Jones] Long-term Tsy futures prices turn higher, recently reading session highs as traders focus on Fed's QE2 Tsy buys rather than doubt market's ability to handle this afternoon's auction of $13 bln in 30-yr Tsy bonds. Mar 10-yr Tsy note futures recently rose to high of 120-28, with resistance seen at Tues' 1-month peak of 121-04. Further upside to 121-20 drops 10-yr cash yield equivalent to 3.25%, says Optima Investment Research. Mar classic Tsy bonds, covering 15 to 25-yr maturities, recently climbed to 121-05 session top. Resistance viewed at Tues' high of 121-18 and Mon's high of 121-21. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1640 GMT [Dow Jones] The Fed tr