\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Euro On Pace For Biggest Gain Since July 1\b0\par\par\uc2 1,345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2011\par 19:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Robert Flint, 212-416-2216; \par robert.flint@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1800 GMT [Dow Jones] The euro is on pace Thursday to post its biggest one-day gain against the dollar since July 1. The euro has been strengthened throughout the day by relatively strong auction results for Spanish and Italian debt, hawkish comments from ECB president Trichet and a disappointing weekly jobless report in the US. The euro is up 1.77% to $1.3363, according to EBS via CQG. That's the common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's biggest gain since July 1 when it rose more than 2.3%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (stephen.bernard@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1759 GMT [Dow Jones]Shortly before $13 billion auction of 30-year Treasurys at 1 p.m. EST, the when-issued 30-year yielded 4.492% at 12:59 p.m. EST, compared to the benchmark issue which yielded 4.487%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1759 GMT [Dow Jones] Some market participants say the run-up in Tsy futures prices due in part to the unexpectedly large Fed purchase of almost $3.8 bln in cash Tsys, set to mature in Dec 2017, or almost 7 yrs from now. In apparent defiance of looming $13 bln 30-yr Tsy bond auction, Mar classic Tsy bond futures price hits one-week high of 121-24. At same time, Mar ultra Tsy bond futures price rises to 124-30 session top. Classic contracts cover 15 to 25 yr maturities. Ultras cover maturities 25 yrs and up. Mar 10-yr Tsy note futures recently reached 121-03 session high, near Tues' 1-month high of 121-04. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1755 GMT [Dow Jones] The rally in SovX Western Europe after this week's successful Portuguese, Spanish, and Italian bond auctions has taken the index back below SovX CEEMA, which trades at 203/204 bps, versus 198.5/200.5 bps on the Western European index, data from Markit show. SovX Western Europe first traded above SovX CEEMEA last week. "The market tone has flipped," says Suki Mann, credit strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1734 GMT [Dow Jones] Bel-20 closes +0.2% at 2633, after a successful Spanish bond auction helps to boost market sentiment, amid talk that euro area finance ministers will take further measures at their meeting next week. Bank stocks benefit most on this change of sentiment: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ageas N.V\f28 \uc2 \f2 . +2.3% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dexia S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 . +1.3%. (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com) Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1734 GMT [Dow Jones] Bel-20 closes +0.2% at 2633, after a successful Spanish bond auction helps to boost market sentiment, amid talk that euro area finance ministers will take further measures at their meeting next week. Bank stocks benefit most on this change of sentiment: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ageas N.V\f28 \uc2 \f2 . +2.3% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dexia S.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 . +1.3%. (riva.froymovich@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1705 GMT [Dow Jones] Following a recent gains for the Peruvian sol, the possibility that the Central Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Peru\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could restart its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to purchase U.S. dollars has increased, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. The sol has rallied in part due to the 25-basis-point increase in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy rate, which now stands at 3.25%. "After the recent surprise hike of 25 bps, USD/PEN spot has rallied sharply to 2.7864 (up 1.2% since December 6). We think the risk that Peru's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will reappear in the market to buy USD is non-negligible (it has not conducted spot purchases since around mid-October). In fact, in past episodes of sharp USD/PEN rallies, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has begun to buy USD only a few days later," it said. (robert.kozak@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The fiscal outlook for Aaa-rated sovereigns is in most cases more positive than that for the four largest Aaa countries--France, Germany, the U.K., and the U.S., Moody's Investors Service said in a report Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Large deficits at smaller Aaa countries are generally temporary, and "a return to a sustainable debt trajectory easily within reach," the rating agency said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canada, the next-largest Aaa country, expects to return to a balanced budged by 2014-2015 and its banking system remains strong, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fiscal metrics for Australia and Singapore, in particular, are among the strongest of Aaa-rated sovereigns, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said, pointing out that Singapore "is currently not in any need of large-scale structural fiscal adjustments."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's debt position "also compares favourably with the [Aaa] group" although the central government's net debt is projected to rise from a low of around 6% of gross domestic product in 2008 to nearly 30% in 2015, before declining.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But these are well below median government debt levels for Aaa countries, and New Zealand's strong banking system means the contingent liability on the government balance sheet is small, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Even with some further slippage... from slower growth or other one-time shocks, it appears highly likely that these ratios will remain within the stronger side of the Aaa range."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Mark Brown, Dow Jones Newswires, + 44 (0)207 842 9485;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 mark.brown@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1700 GMT [Dow Jones] Long-term Tsy futures prices turn higher, recently reading session highs as traders focus on Fed's QE2 Tsy buys rather than doubt market's ability to handle this afternoon's auction of $13 bln in 30-yr Tsy bonds. Mar 10-yr Tsy note futures recently rose to high of 120-28, with resistance seen at Tues' 1-month peak of 121-04. Further upside to 121-20 drops 10-yr cash yield equivalent to 3.25%, says Optima Investment Research. Mar classic Tsy bonds, covering 15 to 25-yr maturities, recently climbed to 121-05 session top. Resistance viewed at Tues' high of 121-18 and Mon's high of 121-21. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1640 GMT [Dow Jones] The Fed trumps ECB today. Treasurys are rallying to session highs after a bout of Fed buying. The market recoup earlier losses made from some comments by Trichet on inflation risks. "The buying was larger than market expectations so bond prices got a nice pop," says Russ Certo, co-head of rate trading at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gleacher & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . In recent trade, the benchmark 10-year note is 7/32 higher to yield 3.338%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1630 GMT [Dow Jones] For about the past week, Eurodollar futures traders have continually priced into the nearby contract reduced fixings for the three-month dollar London Interbank Offered Rate. This reflects reduced fears that ongoing European sovereign debt troubles will tighten interbank credit. Nearby Mar 2011 Eurodollars recently up 1 bp at 99.645, seeing 3-month dollar Libor at 0.355% before Mar. 14 contract expiration. That's down from 0.40% implied rate last Fri. Cash Libor has been unchanged at 0.30313% for the past 5 business days. (howard.packowitz@dowjones.com)\f28 \par 