\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Lower, Sol Slightly Weaker\b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2010\par 22:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock-market indexes ended slightly lower Tuesday on profit-taking and a slight correction on recent gains, said analysts.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General index was down 0.22% to close at 18,995.86. The Selective blue-chip index lost 0.28% to close at 27,566.05, while the key mining subindex fell 0.08%.\par \par \uc2 Losing ground was precious and base metals miner, Minera Corona (MINCORI1), down 1.91% to close at 23.05 soles ($8.30), while Peru's biggest silver producer and fourth-biggest zinc producer, Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLCABC1.VL) lost 2.17% to close at PEN3.60.\par \par \uc2 Going the other way and gaining slightly, despite a dip in gold prices, was precious-metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN, BUENAVC1.VL), up 0.61% to close at $49.10. Also gaining despite volatile red metal prices were copper miners, with \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO, SCCO.VL) up 0.39% to close at $38.65, and Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL), up 1.57% to close at $33.00.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday to buy $73 million at an average of PEN2.7869 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been purchasing dollars regularly since June 18, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol has been on an appreciating trend recently due in part to strong inflows of capital. On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $35 million and Wednesday it bought $38 million.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the sol ended slightly weaker at PEN2.789 per dollar. The sol ended the previous session at PEN2.788 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the sol has appreciated 3.4% against the U.S. dollar, while in the last 12-month period the sol has appreciated 2.4% against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 -By Sophie Kevany, Dow Jones Newswires; 51(1)-989-038-043; sophie.kevany@dowjones.com [ 10-12-10 1629ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101012e6ac000d8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
