\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2010\par 22:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher on Monday, as some key blue chip shares gained ground, especially in the resource extraction sector.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General index closed higher by 0.69%, at 17,435.56.\par \par \uc2 The Selective blue-chip index ended stronger by 0.20% at 25,386.26.\par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) rose 2.0% at end at $30.70.\par \par \uc2 Brokerage Inteligo said it has increased its price target on Cerro Verde to $35.23 per share, due in part to increased reserves.\par \par \uc2 Base metals miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO) increased 0.9% to end at $35.10.\par \par \uc2 Beverage producer Union de Cervecerias Peruanas Backus & Johnston SAA (BACKUSI.VL) increased 1.6% to end at 5.12 soles ($1.84).\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Monday to purchase $139 million at an average of PEN2.7889 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly weaker at PEN2.790 per dollar. In the previous session the sol closed at PEN2.788 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been purchasing dollars regularly since June 18, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol has been on an appreciating trend recently due in part to strong inflows of capital.\par \par \uc2 From the start of the year to Sept. 21 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $7.77 billion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have helped boost \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net international reserves to $42.66 billion as of Sept. 22.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511 - 99927 7269; peru@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -0- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-27-10 1640ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100927e69r000cj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
