\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Colombia  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  buys dollars, peso falls\b0\par\par\uc2 761 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 14:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy at least $20 mln daily\par \par \uc2 * Dollar purchases to start from Wednesday\par \par \uc2 * Accumulation of reserves to last at least four months\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank buys $19.9 mln at its first auction (Recasts; adds peso close, details, comment, byline)\par \par \uc2 By Jack Kimball and Nelson Bocanegra\par \par \uc2 BOGOTA, Sept 15 (Reuters) - Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday started purchasing what it said would be at least $20 million daily for the next four months to help ease the rise of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , becoming the latest Latin American economy to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its market.\par \par \uc2 The move left the door open for more measures to curb the peso's <COP=RR> appreciation and followed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Brazil to ease the real's climb and \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's buying dollars to curb the sol. For details, see [ID:nN10255466] [ID:nN14108242]\par \par \uc2 "The Board of Directors of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to resume the accumulation of international reserves. To do this, it will purchase daily at least $20 million through competitive auctions for at least four months counting from (Wednesday)," the bank said in a statement on its website.\par \par \uc2 The peso, one of the region's strongest performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, fell 1.43 percent to a low of 1,817 pesos per dollar from Tuesday's close after the bank's announcement. The local unit closed down 0.89 percent at 1,807.1 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Colombian peso has soared 12.5 percent against the dollar this year, the sol <PEN=PE> has risen more than 3 percent and the real has rallied 4.5 percent since June. Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened 1 percent on Wednesday after the government threatened to step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Latin America's emerging market economies are struggling with appreciation. Regional powerhouse Brazil is aggressively buying dollars, Peru is tightening deposit requirements and Chile has warned it may also have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $21 million on Wednesday, while on the other side of the world, Japan sold yen to battle an appreciating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which risks reducing demand for exports and damaging growth. For more, see: [ID:nTOE68E02W]\par \par \uc2 The peso's appreciation hurts Colombian exporters, who receive earnings in dollars but pay costs in pesos.\par \par \uc2 MORE MEASURES TO COME\par \par \uc2 Colombia has seen foreign investment in oil and mining boom as its decades-long guerrilla conflict ebbs. The Andean country is now Latin America's No. 4 oil producer and an exporter of coal, coffee, flowers and nickel.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the dollar purchases would help in the short term but could not rule out the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government taking more aggressive steps later in the year. For scenarios on possible measures, click on [ID:nN15183902]\par \par \uc2 Wednesday's "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement was relatively mild, which shows the authorities are still shying away from more forceful \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market direct or indirect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures," said Alberto Ramos of \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Traders said the bank bought $19.9 million at 1,805 pesos per dollar in its first auction on Wednesday after announcing the restart of dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 Between March and June, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $1.6 billion on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but stopped greenback purchases at the end of June.\par \par \uc2 "Surely this announcement will generate volatility and pressures for a rise in the dollar in the short term although it has been shown that this type of action cannot change the structural tendency," Daniel Velandia, manager of economic studies at the brokerage Correval, said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "However, the uncertainty about the amount of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will prevent an important fall of the dollar in the coming days and we continue thinking that if the dollar restarts its falling tendency strongly in the near future, there will be additional measures."\par \par \uc2 Colombia's trade minister, Sergio Diaz Granados, said late on Tuesday that after the government pushes through its fiscal plans, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have room to purchase as much as $9 billion. [ID:nN15156198]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has other options available to stem the peso's rise, including capital controls on short-term portfolio investment, though such measures would not be favored by investors eyeing a return to investment grade for Colombia.\par \par \uc2 "History shows that this may be successful in preventing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating further," Capital Economics said in a report. "But it is unlikely to weaken it substantially -- something the authorities are hoping to achieve." (Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|U|ABX|BNX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100915e69f000um\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
