\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Strengthens\b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2010\par 22:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock-market indexes ended lower Thursday, as a number of precious-metals producing miners lost ground.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General index closed lower by 0.20%, at 15833.44.\par \par \uc2 The Selective blue-chip index ended weaker by 0.44% at 23622.64.\par \par \uc2 Precious-metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) decreased 1.4% to end at $40.31, as the price of gold weakened.\par \par \uc2 Compania Minera Volcan SAA, (VOLCABC1.VL) which is the largest silver producer in Peru, lost 1.0% to end at 3.10 soles ($1.11) as the price of silver eased.\par \par \uc2 Sociedad Minera El Brocal SAA (BROCALC1.VL), one of Peru's leading silver producers, declined 0.3% to end at PEN40.70.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday to purchase $143 million at an average of PEN2.792 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been purchasing dollars regularly since June 18, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol has been on an appreciating trend recently due in part to strong inflows of capital.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the sol ended slightly stronger at PEN2.793 per dollar. In the previous session, the sol closed at PEN2.795 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-99927-7269; peru@dowjones.com [ 09-09-10 1620ET ]\par \par \uc2 