\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Indexes End Higher; Sol Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2010\par 22:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher Monday, boosted by gains in metals prices.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General Index was up 1.12% to close at 15,742.60. The Selective blue-chip index rose 0.95% to close at 23,671.60. The key mining subindex gained 1.25%.\par \par \uc2 Better zinc and tin prices drove gains at zinc-silver miner \uc2 Compania Minera Volcan SA\uc2  (VOLCABC1.VL), up 0.97% to close at 3.13 soles ($1.12), and tin miner \uc2 Minsur SA\uc2  (MINSURI1.VL), up 2.94% to close at PEN7.00.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP) also rose, gaining 0.36% to close at $110.00. Credicorp owns Peru's biggest bank, Banco de Credito.\par \par \uc2 Going the other way on volatile copper prices was base-metals miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO) which lost 0.62%, to close at $31.85.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday to buy $132 million. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been purchasing dollars regularly since June 18, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol has been on an appreciating trend recently due in part to strong inflows of capital. The bank said it paid PEN2.793 to the dollar. Last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $20 million on Tuesday, $171.2 million on Wednesday and $159 million on Friday.\par \par \uc2 On Monday the sol ended unchanged at PEN2.794 per dollar. So far this year the sol has appreciated 3.22% against the U.S. dollar, while in the last 12-month period the sol has appreciated 4.77% against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 -By Sophie Kevany, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-198-903-8043; sophie.kevany@dowjones.com [ 09-06-10 1648ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100906e696000bo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
