\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Strengthens\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2010\par 22:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher Tuesday as a number of key blue-chip shares continued to gain ground.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General Index closed the eighth month of year almost 7% higher for the year, and almost 6% higher than at the end of July.\par \par \uc2 Market analysts expect lackluster trading volumes, with the stock market to be driven by changes in metals prices, movements in international stock markets and appetite for shares tied to Peru's robust economic growth.\par \par \uc2 "Things have been slow here. Until the international scenario becomes clearer, there isn't expected to be much change," said Juan Magot & Asociados SAB trader, Walter Serrano.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the Lima Stock Exchange's broad General index closed higher by 0.31% at 15153.33.\par \par \uc2 The Selective blue-chip index ended stronger by 0.54% at 22807.56.\par \par \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the stock market were closed on Monday for a national holiday.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, precious metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) increased 1.8% to end at $41.01, as the price of gold gained.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP) rose 0.8% to end at $105.00. It owns Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito.\par \par \uc2 Base metals miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO) increased 0.4% to end at $30.17.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday to purchase $20 million.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been purchasing dollars regularly since June 18, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol has been on an appreciating trend recently due, in part, to strong inflows of capital.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the sol ended slightly stronger at PEN2.798 per dollar. In the previous session the sol closed at PEN2.799 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 In the last 12-month period the sol has appreciated 5.35% against the greenback. So far this year the sol has appreciated 3.08%.\par \par \uc2 Peru's finance ministry said in its latest multiyear macroeconomic report that it expects the sol to average PEN2.83 per U.S. dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-99927-7269; peru@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -0- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 31-08-10 2041GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100831e68v001aq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
