\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market, Buys $121 Mln\b0\par\par\uc2 150 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2010\par 20:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday to buy $121 million.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been purchasing dollars regularly since June 18, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. On Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $219.6 million, on Wednesday it bought $102.5 million and on Thursday it bought $3 million.\par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly weaker Friday, at PEN2.801 per dollar. The sol ended the previous session at PEN2.800 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 So far this year the sol has appreciated 2.98% against the U.S. dollar, while in the last 12-month period the sol has appreciated 5.31% against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 -By Sophie Kevany, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-198-903-8043; sophie.kevany@dowjones.com [ 20-08-10 1853GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100820e68k00109\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
