\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-ANALYSIS-Latam seen stepping up  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 , but risk\b0\par\par\uc2 950 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2010\par 14:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Repeats Tuesday story with no changes to text or headline)\par \par \uc2 * Central banks seen stepping in to tame \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally\par \par \uc2 * Colombia, Chile seen joining concrete action\par \par \uc2 * Curbing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could slow rate up-cycle\par \par \uc2 By Simon Gardner\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Aug 17 (Reuters) - South American policymakers will likely step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem surging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, but they tread a fine line that risks fueling inflation and could even put the brakes on a regional rate up-cycle.\par \par \uc2 Lured by higher interest rates and economic growth amid a faltering recovery in the United States and Europe, foreign investors are betting on the region's commodity powerhouses. Dollar inflows are boosting \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and hurting exporters.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year to buy nearly $6 billion to soak up excess liquidity, while the finance ministry said last week it would buy $500 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by year-end to temper its sol <PEN=PE> \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is at 2-year highs.\par \par \uc2 Brazil called an auction on Tuesday to buy dollars on the spot market in a bid to boost reserves and limit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility. [ID:nN16270408]\par \par \uc2 The presidents of Chile and Colombia have both signaled concern about sharp gains in their countries' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely not be enough.\par \par \uc2 "I think the central banks will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily. The central banks that have not yet come in, will. That means Colombia and Chile," said Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, a strategist at RBS Securities.\par \par \uc2 "The problem with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is that the global environment is still very fragile." <------------------------------------------------------ For a graphics, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/ged55n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/ged55n }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/wex55n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/wex55n }}}\uc2  For Chile peso scenarios, see [ID:nN17124678] ------------------------------------------------------->\par \par \uc2 Policymakers could opt to buy dollars to boost international reserves, tax imports or offer incentives to exporters to help counter \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation.\par \par \uc2 They could also raise deposit requirements to help curb money supply, or raise the overnight rate on interbank loans in dollars.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say Chile is likely to delay the rate at which it repatriates hundreds of millions of dollars to help fund reconstruction after a massive February earthquake.\par \par \uc2 RATE UP-CYCLE TO SLOW?\par \par \uc2 Chile joined a regional rate up-cycle led by Peru and Brazil after keeping its key rate at a record low to help the economy recover from the quake and global crisis. But taming \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may slow the pace of future hikes in the region.\par \par \uc2 "By \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market buying dollars you throw pesos into the system (via bonds) and that will eventually generate inflationary pressures," said Alfredo Coutino, Latin America director at \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Economy.com.\par \par \uc2 "I don't see a future for a continuous (rate) heightening cycle in Latin America," he added, saying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely slow the pace of interest rate increases.\par \par \uc2 Chilean President Sebastian Pinera said on Thursday he would use all macroeconomic tools to keep the country's peso <CLP=CL> competitive, but after a brief retracement, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to surge near 7-month highs. For more, see [ID:nN12124343]\par \par \uc2 The same day, Colombian President Juan Manuel Santos met with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to discuss the strength of the country's peso <COP=RR>, which is up around 10 percent against the dollar year-to-date. [ID:nN12123476]\par \par \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year has sought to squeeze speculative capital out by raising deposit requirements on dollar loans from abroad and local bank accounts denominated in dollars. [ID:nN18173256]\par \par \uc2 Despite heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol is up nearly 3 percent so far this year at around 2.8 per dollar, and the market sees it appreciating by another 1.0 to 2.0 percent by year-end.\par \par \uc2 In neighboring Chile, investors expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars if the peso, which has surged over 3 percent in August alone, firms toward around 480 per dollar. The peso is now 1.0 percent higher year-to-date.\par \par \uc2 During the 2008 commodity boom that pushed the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 430 pesos per dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began buying dollars on the local market to build up its reserves and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened sharply by the year-end. It then rebounded by more than 26 percent in 2009.\par \par \uc2 Chilean exporters are feeling the pinch, and want action.\par \par \uc2 "Producers are really affected by exchange rate variations and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ensure stability would be positive," said Miguel Montenegro, manager of Chilean berry exporter Blue Valley. Chile is the world's leading copper producer and is also a major fruit, wood pulp and salmon exporter.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real's <BRBY> sharp appreciation has also hit exporters. But traders continue to test 1.75 per dollar, even after the government voiced support for a weaker real.\par \par \uc2 Doug Smith, head of Latin American research at Standard Chartered in New York, expects more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- whoever wins an Oct. 3 presidential election -- via verbal warnings, double spot auctions or reverse swaps.\par \par \uc2 However, nothing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do will come as much of a surprise to major players in the market, says Joao Medeiros, a partner at Pioneer Corretora, one of Brazils biggest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokerages.\par \par \uc2 "The market is like a game of poker but one in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can see everyones cards," he said. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could do up to 10 auctions in one day if it needed to but it won't. It has everything under control." (Additional reporting by Samantha Pearson in Sao Paulo, Terry Wade in Lima and Brad Haynes and Alonso Soto in Santiago; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ANALYSIS) (REPEAT)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|ABX|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100821e68i0006b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
