\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes Down; Sol Weakens A Bit\b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2010\par 22:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended lower Friday, dragged down by weakness in international markets and lower copper prices.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General index fell 0.32% to close at 14,699.98. The Selective blue-chip index lost 0.70% to close at 21,977.93, while the mining subindex was down 0.76%.\par \par \uc2 Losing ground was red metal miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO, SCCO.VL), down 1.13% to close at $30.70. Also down was fellow copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL), losing 1.63% to close at $24.10.\par \par \uc2 Base metals miner \uc2 Compania Minera Milpo\uc2  SAA (MILPOC1.VL) lost 1.00% to close at 6.93 soles ($2.47).\par \par \uc2 Going the other way on higher gold prices was precious metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN, BUENAVC1) which rose 0.39% to close at $36.50.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday to purchase $167 million.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been purchasing dollars regularly since June 18, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. On Monday it purchased $95 million, while on Tuesday it bought $149.5 million. On Wednesday it purchased $107 million, while on Thursday it purchased another $200 million.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the sol ended slightly weaker at PEN2.802 per dollar. In the previous session the sol closed at PEN2.801 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Late Thursday the Central Reserve Bank of Peru increased its reference interest rate by 50 basis points to 2.5%.\par \par \uc2 "Further interest rate rises look likely and will maintain the upward pressure of the PEN [+3% against the USD since the start of the year]. As in the recent past, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try and cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciating trend is likely to do little more than slow the rate of PEN gains," RBC Emerging Markets Research said in a note.\par \par \uc2 -By Sophie Kevany, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-198-903-8043; sophie.kevany@dowjones.com [ 08-06-10 1645ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100806e686000ch\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
