\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2010\par 23:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock-market indexes ended slightly higher Friday. Traders said the Lima exchange was lifted by a rise in copper prices, positive sentiment in U.S. markets and upbeat second-quarter results from a local property company.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General index rose 0.73% to close at 14,152.01, while the Selective blue-chip index gained 0.72%, closing at 21,308.05. The mining subindex rose 0.81%.\par \par \uc2 Gaining value were copper miners Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL), which rose 0.47% to close at $23.61, and \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (SCCO), which was up 0.31% at $32.10.\par \par \uc2 The Southern Copper price fluctuated during the day following news that parent company Grupo Mexico SAB (GMEXICO.MX) was proposing to merge Southern Copper with \uc2 Asarco LLC\uc2 , a Grupo Mexico subsidiary.\par \par \uc2 Going the other way on lower gold prices was precious metals mining company \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN), down 0.43% to close at $39.40.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday to buy $160 million. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been purchasing dollars regularly since June 18 to ease volatility in the exchange market.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $240 million, and on Monday it bought $120 million. Bulltick Research said Friday in a report that Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought $4.8 billion this year up to Thursday to "keep appreciation pressures at bay." As a point of comparison, Bulltick said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought a high of $10.3 billion in 2007.\par \par \uc2 The sol ended unchanged Friday at PEN2.824 per dollar. So far this year, the sol has appreciated 2.18% against the U.S. dollar, while in the last 12-month period the sol has appreciated 5.74% against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 -By Sophie Kevany, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-198-903-8043; sophie.kevany@dowjones.com [ 23-07-10 2115GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100723e67n001fd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
