\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes A Bit Lower; Sol Is Stronger\b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2010\par 22:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended slightly lower Friday. Traders blamed losses on external market slippage this week, despite Peru's strong economic indicators and higher metals prices. "Investors are risk averse--there is a pessimistic mood," said Sebastian Blondet, of Celfin Capital.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General index lost 0.08% to close at 13,823.92. The Selective blue-chip index fell 0.42% to close at 20,449.75.\par \par \uc2 Tin miner \uc2 Minsur SA\uc2  (MINSURI1.VL) was down 1.26% to close at 6.25 soles ($2.22), while base-metals miner \uc2 Compania Minera Milpo\uc2  SAA (MILPOC1.VL) lost 0.29%, closing at PEN6.95. Maple Energy (MPLE.LN), which has oil, gas and ethanol projects in Peru, also lost 2.94% to close at $0.66.\par \par \uc2 Going the other way, boosted by better precious metals prices was gold and silver miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN), up 0.24% to close at $37.00. Silver miner Sociedad Minera El Brocal SAA. (BROCALC1.VL), also gained 1.16% to close at PEN43.50, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) rose 0.84% to close at $22.80.\par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday to buy $25 million. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in every trading session since June 18. The Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. On Friday the sol ended slightly stronger at PEN2.825 per dollar, compared with PEN2.826 per dollar in the previous trading session.\par \par \uc2 -By Sophie Kevany, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-198-903-8043; sophie.kevany@dowjones.com [ 07-02-10 1641ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100702e672000c2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
