\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Sharply Lower; Sol Strengthens\b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2010\par 22:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended sharply lower Thursday, as various blue chip shares again declined.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General index ended 1.61% weaker at 14,811.10.\par \par \uc2 The Selective blue-chip index ended 2.12% lower at 23,490.47.\par \par \uc2 The mining subindex fell 1.80%\par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (PCU) continued to decline, ending 5.38% lower at $30.80 as copper prices weakened.\par \par \uc2 Precious-metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura SA\uc2 , (BUENAVC1.VL) finished 5.66% weaker at 92.45 soles ($32.44).\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP) fell 0.54% to end at $73.60. It owns Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the sol ended slightly stronger at PEN2.850 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at PEN2.854 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 So far this year the sol has appreciated 1.28% against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, following nine consecutive trading session in which it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy U.S. dollars in order to ease the appreciation of the sol.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy about $1.4 billion recently are a signal that it doesn't want a significant appreciation of the sol, \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  said in a report.\par \par \uc2 "We expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if capital inflows remain high; with the economy still weak and inflation low, we do not think that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is concerned about the expansion of the monetary aggregates," it said.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511 - 99927 7269; peru@dowjones.com [ 01-21-10 1631ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100121e61l000fc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
