\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Chief: Dec GDP Growth Could Reach 5%\b0\par\par\uc2 244 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2010\par 21:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's Central Reserve Bank president, Julio Velarde, forecast on Tuesday that December's gross domestic product growth figure could register slightly over 5%, bringing the total 2009 GDP figure to "about 1%."\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a press conference Tuesday, Velarde also suggested the consumer price index would rise in January, mainly due to recent fuel price increases.\par \par \uc2 Although Velarde said the bank saw no substantial short-term inflationary pressures, and would maintain its current low reference interest rate, he warned of a possible increase in supply-side prices.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aims to keep inflation at between 1% and 3%. In December, the country's benchmark consumer price index, used to set monetary policy, rose 0.32% from the previous month, bringing the annual increase in the CPI to 0.25%.\par \par \uc2 Asked if the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market would continue, Velarde said yes, "up to a certain limit." He would not specify what the limit is, however.\par \par \uc2 Since Jan. 8, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has purchased about $1.3 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy $285.5 million.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market.\par \par \uc2 -By Sophie Kevany, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-198-903-8043; sophie.kevany@dowjones.com [ 01-19-10 1509ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020100119e61j000k5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
