\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Stronger\b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2010\par 22:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended higher Monday, for the sixth straight session, boosted by higher metals prices and investor confidence.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General index ended up 1.89% to close at 15,924.80.\par \par \uc2 The Selective blue-chip index was up 2.18% to close at 25,743.03. The mining index rose 0.54%.\par \par \uc2 Traders said factors driving the stock market included higher prices for copper, zinc, gold and silver, as well as investor confidence leading up to the publication of annual financial results.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted gains in the industry, electricity and energy sectors, as well as in metals and mining.\par \par \uc2 Leading the gains Monday was Maple Energy (MPLE.LN), which rose a sharp 14.52%, to close at $1.42, following Friday's news of further loan approvals for its Peruvian ethanol project.\par \par \uc2 In the mining sector, \uc2 Compania Minera Atacocha SA\uc2 's B shares (ATACOBC1.VL) gained 3.59% in heavy trade to close at 2.02 soles ($0.72).\par \par \uc2 Steel products company \uc2 Empresa Siderurgica del Peru\uc2  (SIDERC1.VL) rose 1.48% to close at PEN1.35.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Intergroup Financial Services Corp\uc2 . (IFS.VL), also gained sharply, up 5.26% to close at $23.00 following the appointment of a new interim general manager.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy $184 million. This followed its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $323 million on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the exchange market. Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol ended stronger at PEN2.851 per U.S. dollar. The sol ended the previous session at PEN2.853 per U.S. dollar. So far this year, the sol has appreciated 1.25% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Sophie Kevany, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-198-903-8043; sophie.kevany@dowjones.com [ 01-11-10 1653ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100111e61b000e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
