\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  To Buy U.S. Dollars\b0\par\par\uc2 983 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2010\par 18:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York.  Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1748 GMT [Dow Jones] The Central Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Peru intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy U.S. dollars in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on Friday, an official with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a conference call, without giving an amount. The Peruvian sol has gained almost 0.9% against the greenback so far this year. (RSK)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1747 GMT [Dow Jones] One new high-grade bond on tap Friday - a triple-A rated 10-year from \uc2 Rabobank Nederland\uc2  - while supply is expected to pick up next week. Spreads remain in range. The benchmark high-grade credit derivatives index, the Markit CDX IG13, is quoted 1 bp tighter at 78 bps on Tradeweb.(RV)\par \par \uc2 1723 GMT [Dow Jones] Investors who do not buy Greek government bonds, "are likely to underperform their indexes for the moment," says \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 . Most of the bad news for Greece now is out, SG says, adding "we believe we are facing 6-12 months with few negative news developments." SG notes that funding pressures have eased for Greece for 2010, and while yield spreads are still wide, carry is "too generous." SG says whilst there will be ructions in 2011 if the Papandreou government doesn't get to grips with public spending, this is a distant risk. (BEM)\par \par \uc2 1720 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD is gaining some steam after paring its gains earlier as an unexpected increase in US wholesale inventories cast the US economy in a brighter light amid disappointment over payrolls data. EUR/USD now at 1.4371 from 1.4320 late Thu, according to EBS via CQG. (BMD)\par \par \uc2 1719 GMT [Dow Jones] German inflation-linked federal bond, bundei April 2020, on auction Wednesday, looks attractive from the investor's view point, says \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 , adding that it's almost 43 basis points cheaper than the corresponding nominal. SG adds that the paper is also cheap in break-even terms, trading at 188.5 basis points versus 203 basis points for the French peer OATei July 2020. (BEM)\par \par \uc2 1718 GMT [Dow Jones] Fitch maintained its "A" rating and stable outlook for $5.3 bln of Puerto Rico Sales Tax Financing Corp. sales tax revenue bonds and assigned that ranking also to as much as $2.2 bln of new bonds that the corporation may sell around Jan. 19. The ratings firm also affirmed its "A"-plus rating on $5.2 bln of outstanding senior lien bonds. Ratings on both classes of bonds reflect a structure and revenue pledge that insulates them from the strained general fund \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the commonwealth, Fitch said. The bonds also provide solid current debt coverage, and legal opinions are strong, the firm said. (SDR)\par \par \uc2 1713 GMT [Dow Jones] Price talk on \uc2 Rabobank Nederland\uc2 's 10-year note is around 95 bps over Tsys, according to a person familiar with the deal. Size at least $500M through private placement. The note, via \uc2 Barclays\uc2 /\uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 /\uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 /\uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 , is expected to price later Friday. (AAA/AAA)(RV)\par \par \uc2 1700 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  says a lot of choppy trading over the past few hours is muddying the near-term outlook for USD/CAD, but it still thinks the underlying trend remains lower. Resistance has dropped to 1.0380 while support stands at 1.0295, and those levels define the short-term range, TD says. "There remains some risk of a pop to the mid 1.04 area but that should be the extent of USD strength if the underlying downtrend is to prevail in the next week or so," it says. USD currently around 1.0350 vs CAD. (DBC)\par \par \uc2 1659 GMT0 [Dow Jones] Expectations for mid-year increase in fed-funds rate diminishes further in fed-funds futures. July contract now prices in only 16% chance for FOMC to lift funds rate to 0.5% at late June meeting. That's down from 30% chance just before release of this morning's weaker-than-expected jobs report. July contract's price recently up 4 BP at 99.71. (HLP)\par \par \uc2 1657 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Moody's\uc2  upgrade of Turkey "reduces the government's need for external policy anchors in the form of an IMF program, especially as the 2011 elections draw closer," says Ahmet Akarli of \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 . Akarli adds that the upgrade is deserved, particularly given Turkey's macro fundamentals. "We expect S&P to follow with a similar one-notch upgrade in the near future," Akarli adds. (CAC)\par \par \uc2 1654 GMT [Dow Jones] While a lot of cash investors are no longer relying on TALF funds to buy auto or credit card ABS, some off-the-run sectors like dealer floorplan are still reliant "to some degree on TALF," say Citi analysts in a note. "Spreads for these off-the-run sectors could widen when the TALF program expires," they note, adding the Fed "might consider retaining a contingency facility at higher spreads and haircuts to maintain market access for the off-the-run sectors." The consumer loan-backed portion of TALF is set to expire in March. (ASH)\par \par \uc2 1654 GMT [Dow Jones] Volatilities implied by USD/JPY \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options were lower in NY Fri from Tokyo after the dollar fell against the yen. One-month at-the-money USD/JPY options implied volatilities were at 12.60%/13.30%, from 12.95%/13.65% in Tokyo and from 12.45%/13.15% Thu in NY. One-month EUR/USD implied vols were at 10.20%/10.60%, from 10.45%/10.85% in Tokyo and from 10.50%/10.90% Thu in NY. One-month EUR/JPY implied vols were at 11.75%/12.55% from 11.80%/12.60% in Tokyo and from 11.90%/12.70% in NY Thu. (BMD) [ 01-08-10 1250ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100108e618000d7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
