\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ Peru's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Wants Limits On Banks' Dollar Holdings\b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2009\par 17:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from superintendent spokesman and economists, additional comments from Velarde, in sixth through 10th paragraphs; \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves in last paragraph) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Robert Kozak \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--The Central Reserve Bank of Peru wants to have a limit placed on local bank holdings of U.S. dollars, aiming to cut down on exchange market volatility.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to reduce to 50% the maximum limit on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that local banks can hold in net long positions from the current 100%.\par \par \uc2 "This is a regulation aimed at a prudent management on the macro level and isn't aimed at any one entity, but rather at ensuring the health of the economy," Central Reserve Bank President Julio Velarde said in a statement released Saturday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the current 100% limit contributes to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volatility.\par \par \uc2 Velarde said setting a limit of 50% would bring that to a level similar to the amount of dollarization in the Peruvian economy. The U.S. dollar is legal tender in Peru and is widely used.\par \par \uc2 The nation's Superintendent of Banking and Insurance would have to change the limits on bank holdings, a spokesman for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday.\par \par \uc2 Velarde noted that other nations in the region, such as Colombia and Chile, currently have limits on local bank holdings of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Economists say the proposed measure wouldn't affect Peruvian banks much right now, as for the most part they are reducing U.S. dollar positions.\par \par \uc2 "It wouldn't be any problem if it were introduced right now," said Hugo Perea, chief economist for BBVA Banco Continental.\par \par \uc2 The measure could take on greater importance for some banks if the current trend toward a strengthening sol were reduced and in a period of volatility the sol began to weaken, economists pointed out.\par \par \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also wants to establish a maximum limit of from 40% to 50% in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings, without coverage, for private pension funds.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said this would also reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk and volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Currently there is no limit on the investments in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the private pension funds, although those funds are limited in how much they can invest outside of Peru.\par \par \uc2 Banco BBVA Continental said in a report that as of Sept. 30, the private pension funds had 37.6% of their portfolios in U.S. dollars.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent weeks to stem volatility in the exchange market tied to strong demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol. In the 2007 to 2009 period, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought an accumulated $13.17 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-99927 7269; \b \highlight22\uc2 peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 @dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 02, 2009 11:29 ET (16:29 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020091102e5b200491\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
