\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Peru's Sol Seen On Appreciating Trend\b0\par\par\uc2 862 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2009\par 16:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in New York. Darlene Ross, 212 416-2166; \par darlene.ross@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1436 GMT [Dow Jones] Global and domestic conditions still appear to favour an appreciation of the Peruvian sol, barring a surprise correction in global equities markets, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said, adding that this likely means increased \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Peru\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy U.S. dollars. "With the risk of increased USD buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , we see room for some consolidation in the short term around 2.90/USD. However, we now expect net inflows to drive the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  toward 2.85/USD by year-end and to 2.75/USD by mid-2010." (RSK)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1435 GMT[Dow Jones] The initial price talk on Freddie's 2-year note is at Treasury's plus 26 bps, according to Jim Vogel of FTN Financial. "The pricing could make it clearly more attractive than our former favorite in this sector, the Fannie 2s of Jan. 2012," he said. (NPN)\par \par \uc2 1431 GMT [Dow Jones] Overnight repo market showing strain on supply of current 2- and 5-yr notes. They're both quoted at 0.05%, well below the 0.19% general collateral rate. Fed funds traded 0.13%. All quotes from GovPx. (ECB)\par \par \uc2 1428 GMT [Dow Jones] Dollar is slipping gradually lower as stocks stay supported in early trading and aid risk appetites. EUR/USD has moved higher to $1.4943 from $1.4885 late Fri, while USD/JPY has faded to Y90.55 from Y90.87. DJIA up over 50 pts. (PE)\par \par \uc2 1428 GMT [Dow Jones] Short- and long-term rate futures prices turn positive, reaching intraday highs as NY Fed says reverse repo testing has no monetary policy implications. Quarterly 2010-11 Eurodollar futures recently up as much as 3 BP. Long-term Dec 10-yr Tsy note and 30-yr bond contracts each surpass Fri's highs. Dec 10-yrs climb to 118-10+, and Dec 30-yr bonds rise to 119-29. (HLP)\par \par \uc2 1427 GMT [Dow Jones] ICAP's US quotes on interbank lending are mixed Monday, with the 1-mo New York funding rate down at 0.2338% from 0.2375% Fri, and the 3-mo rate up at 0.2981% from 0.2963%. That's widened the gap to the UK benchmark. Earlier in the UK, the BBA quoted 3-mo dollar Libor down at 0.28338% from 0.28406% Fri. (ECB)\par \par \uc2 1425 GMT [Dow Jones] Hungarian government bonds are largely unchanged after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 50 basis point rate cut to 7%, as the move was widely expected, a trader says. Levels are also steady from Friday. Trader expects Hungarian bonds to be moved by global markets in the next few days. "Even the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's communication was in line with expectations," he says. "They are biased towards a possible cut but the global sentiment can change this any time." The three-year bond yields at 6.83%, five-year at 6.96%, 10-year at 7.20%. The forint firms versus the euro to between 265.50 and 266 from 267 at opening. (BEM)\par \par \uc2 1421 GMT [Dow Jones] Treasurys prices lifting faster now as traders cover shorts they'd put on earlier amid anxiety that the Fed's trials of reverse repos means a rate hike is in the wings. The NY Fed's press release just now, saying the tests "have no monetary policy implications," is getting through, says \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  head of Tsys Rick Klingman. Two-yr is up 1/32 yielding 0.96%, 10-yr is 8/32 higher for 3.39%.(ECB)\par \par \uc2 1403 GMT [Dow Jones] Public utility holding company \uc2 Southern Company\uc2  (A3/A-) is in the market with a $300M offering of 2-year FRNs via joint lead managers Deutsche/RBS. The deal is expected to be priced later Monday. (KAG)\par \par \uc2 1402 GMT [Dow Jones] Analysts say trade in emerging market debt is muted ahead of key \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meetings this week, including in Hungary, Brazil and South Africa. (RFO)\par \par \uc2 1401 GMT [Dow Jones] Euro-denominated government bonds remain down after attempting to recover from the day's lows. Amid little data, the market has been driven by stronger equities as last week's risk appetite momentum extends. European government bond peripherals outperformed German ones, another sign of improving optimism. Looking ahead, earnings reports continue this week and the Fed's Bernanke and Kohn are due to speak later Monday. Tuesday brings German September PPI at 0600 GMT, with US September housing starts and US PPI at 1230 GMT. The bund yield curve steepens, with the 2-year/10-year benchmark spread widening to +188.3bp from Friday's +185.9bp. The December bund futures contract is currently down 0.20 on the day at 121.26. The 10-year benchmark bund is down 0.26 at 101.62, yielding 3.301%. (NKA)\par \par \uc2 1401 GMT [Dow Jones] Agency mortgage bonds are weaker, continuing their weakening trend. Investors last week abandoned the current coupon in preference for higher coupons. Risk premiums are 1 bp wider to Tsys at 147 bps. (NPN) [ 10-19-09 1036ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020091019e5aj000bk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
