\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stocks End Lower; Sol Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2009\par 23:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock market indexes ended lower Monday, as some key mining companies declined.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's broad General index ended down 0.58% to close at 15,349.45.\par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index fell 0.86% to close at 24,744.04.\par \par \uc2 The mining index closed 0.59% lower.\par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) ended down 5.66% to close at $36.84, in heavy trade.\par \par \uc2 Workers at two Buenaventura mines walked out on Monday as part of protests called by the National Mining Federation to pressure the government to improve benefits.\par \par \uc2 Gold miner \uc2 Minera IRL Ltd\uc2  (MIRL) also ended 0.88% lower to close at $1.14.\par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (PCU) ended the session up 2.32%, to close at $35.30, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) ended up 0.91% to close at $24.30, on stronger copper prices.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy $92 million.\par \par \uc2 With the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol ended unchanged on Monday at 2.855 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Global and domestic conditions still appear to favor an appreciation of the Peruvian sol, barring a surprise correction in global equities markets, \uc2 HSBC\uc2  said, adding that this likely means increased \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy U.S. dollars.\par \par \uc2 "With the risk of increased USD buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we see room for some consolidation in the short term around 2.90/USD," it added. "However, we now expect net inflows to drive the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  toward 2.85/USD by year-end and to 2.75/USD by mid-2010."\par \par \uc2 -By Sophie Kevany and Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-99927 7269; peru@dowjones.com [ 10-19-09 1705ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020091019e5aj000f3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
