\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Stock Indexes End With Gains; Sol Strengthens\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2008\par 22:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended higher Thursday, lifted by a gain in blue chip shares.\par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index increased 0.35% to end at 7,743.13.\par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip rose 0.30% to finish at 12,834.41.\par \par \uc2 Miner Southern Copper Corp. (PCU) ended 17.0% higher at $14.98.\par \par \uc2 That is still sharply down from its 52-week high of $41.93.\par \par \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 , (BAP) Peru's largest financial holding company, rose 5.1% to end at $42.31. The share's 52-week high was $86.91.\par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) gained 11.7% to end at 42.32 soles ($13.65).\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell $232 million.\par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly stronger, at PEN3.1030 per U.S. dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at PEN3.1040 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 In a report, Banco de Credito said that "in the coming days, the exchange rate could continue to show important fluctuations, in line with the release of indicators in the United States and other industrialized nations."\par \par \uc2 It said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to continue selling U.S. dollars in order to smooth out \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-21